WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.602
Strong analysis uses language that matches the strength of the evidence.

00:00:04.602 --> 00:00:09.707
If West has the highest mean in this sample, say exactly that.

00:00:09.707 --> 00:00:17.172
Do not turn a sample pattern into a universal statement such as West customers always spend more.

00:00:17.172 --> 00:00:23.547
Similarly, if two variables are correlated, say they are associated in the data.

00:00:23.547 --> 00:00:26.911
Do not automatically say that one causes the other.

00:00:27.696 --> 00:00:32.103
Words matter because they communicate how certain the conclusion is.

00:00:32.103 --> 00:00:38.508
Phrases such as in this sample, appears higher, is associated with,

00:00:38.508 --> 00:00:43.548
or may indicate are often appropriate for descriptive analysis.

00:00:43.548 --> 00:00:48.248
Causal claims require stronger study designs, assumptions, and evidence.

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:53.298
A good analyst is not someone who makes the strongest statement possible.

00:00:53.298 --> 00:00:59.673
A good analyst makes the strongest statement that the evidence actually supports.
